  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $z$ be a complex number such that $|z|+z=3+i$\r\n\r\n$($ where $i=\\sqrt{-1})$\r\n\r\nThen $|\\mathrm{z}|$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Lb7jH",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bmoPs",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oLZAf",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7A9Vs",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, $|z|+z=3+i$\r\n\r\nLet $z=a+i b,$ then\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n|z|+z=3+i \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}+a+i b=3+i\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nCompare real and imaginary coefficients on both sides\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\nb=1, \\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}+a=3 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\sqrt{a^{2}+1}=3-a \\\\\r\n\r\na^{2}+1=a^{2}+9-6 a \\\\\r\n\r\n6 a=8 \\Rightarrow a=\\frac{4}{3}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nThen,\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n|z|=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^{2}+1}=\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{9}+1}=\\frac{5}{3}\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
